<title>USA: Mobil share price up as beats forecasts.</title>
<headline>Mobil share price up as beats forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Mobil Corp rallied 3/8 to 126-1/4 after the company reported first quarter net operating income per share of $2.11, up from $1.83 a year ago and ahead of analysts' forecasts of $2.02, according to First Call.</p>
<p>Phillips Petroleum, where net operating income was a penny per share below forecasts at $0.94 from $0.80 was off 3/8 at 38-1/8.</p>
<p>Chevron Corp was up 7/8 at 67-1/2 after net operating income per share came in at $1.27 against $0.94 and a First Call consensus of $1.13. ((--New York Newsroom 212 859 1902))</p>
</text>
